[{:db/id 17592186162071 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7843f1c8-1167-5bc2-84a4-7db8f3081808"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162102 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9bb0375a-c98d-553b-9152-a70fe8a2eeb1" "question-3cc02d81-9348-594e-8ded-6e3235e0303a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161872 :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f_X(x)$ and $f_Y(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.25}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.35$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.5}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.25}$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $0.35$ | $0.65$ | $1$ |\n\nThe marginal mass function for $X$ is given in the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ | $0.25$ |\n\nFinally, using the table of values of the marginal mass function for $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & =P(X\\in \\{2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =0.5+0.25 \\\\  & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-7843f1c8-1167-5bc2-84a4-7db8f3081808" :question/id #uuid "7843f1c8-1167-5bc2-84a4-7db8f3081808" :question/math-academy-id "q-142567" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ below for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find ${f}_{X}(3).$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.35$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.35$ | $0.3$ | $0.35$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(3) & =f(3,0)+f(3,1)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =0.2+0.1+0.05 \\\\  & =0.35.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f9f24a0a-a03d-56b3-b962-7005c236dd29"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f9f24a0a-a03d-56b3-b962-7005c236dd29" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9f24a0a-a03d-56b3-b962-7005c236dd29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2e02ef30-7705-5bf7-ae13-d466e60d3409" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c8f5f9e3-2ce5-5e18-b115-a3bc9bec3641" "answer-2e02ef30-7705-5bf7-ae13-d466e60d3409" "answer-49227992-7dad-5c8e-8853-4765f7f38dc7" "answer-75066fec-23f7-5ab3-a28a-b3a3c440ffe2" "answer-2da33fc0-18c6-5b5b-9178-dc0d38d868b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8f5f9e3-2ce5-5e18-b115-a3bc9bec3641" :answer/id #uuid "c8f5f9e3-2ce5-5e18-b115-a3bc9bec3641" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3" :db/ens